Create an exactly 15-second live-action cinematic scene, landscape 16:9, beginning a quiet contemporary Vietnamese relationship drama. Exactly two featured adults appear. They are acquaintances who have met a few times, not close friends or an established couple. REFERENCES: Preserve the photographed identities, facial proportions, skin tones, physiques, hairstyles, approved clothing, and accessories. Reference-sheet poses and expressions are not fixed performances: allow believable emotional changes while retaining identity. Environment images describe one continuous location, not interchangeable backgrounds. Never display reference panels, mannequins, swatches, or studio backgrounds. VISUAL STYLE: Real actors filmed on location with natural facial asymmetry, fine skin texture, realistic eyes, irregular individual hair strands, and fabric with visible weave and weight. Avoid beauty filters, waxy skin, sculpted hair, stylized faces, and game-like rendering. NIGHT LIGHTING: Use soft cool moonlight from one consistent direction and restrained neutral fill that keeps faces readable without looking like daytime. Preserve natural skin color, gentle shadow transitions, dark surroundings, and small distant warm lights. Stars remain distant background detail, not glittering effects. GEOGRAPHY: The woman sits directly on grass beside the staircase’s middle landing, clear of the steps, facing the river. Her handbag and phone rest within reach beside her outer hip, away from the staircase. The man approaches along the upper dyke path and descends toward that landing. Keep the staircase, shoreline, and paths fixed across views. 0.00–5.00s: Open in a wide three-quarter view from slightly above the woman’s seated level. Place her prominently in the lower-right area and the approaching man farther back toward the left. Use natural 35mm-equivalent perspective. Her knees rest together, legs comfortably angled downslope, dress arranged according to its actual construction. She wipes one cheek with her fingertips and tries to steady her breathing. He walks at an ordinary pace in the background. Slowly move the camera forward, preserving both characters and their spatial relationship. 5.00–8.00s: Cut to an eye-level medium shot of the man as he notices her. His pace slows, shoulders settle, and his expression changes from relaxed to uncertain recognition. He stops at the upper landing, looks down toward her, and says in Vietnamese: “Linh?” Deliver it as a quiet question, not a shout. 8.00–15.00s: Cut over his shoulder toward her, keeping his shoulder softly visible and her face sharp. She turns toward his voice, recognizes him, quickly wipes beneath her eye, and says: “Ơ… anh Minh.” After her response, he asks gently: “Sao em ngồi đây?” She looks away briefly and replies: “Em ra hóng gió tí.” Allow natural short pauses between speakers. Her voice carries slight recent crying but the words remain clear. During the final second, he begins stepping down toward her; she returns her gaze toward the river. End with that descent continuing. PERFORMANCE AND PHYSICS: Restrained blinks, small gaze changes, uneven breathing, and subtle facial transitions. Do not make her cry theatrically throughout. Her seated weight compresses grass; clothing gathers naturally around hips and knees. Shoes contact individual steps without skating. A light consistent breeze moves loose hair, hems, and grass with delayed settling. AUDIO: Quiet insects, wind, river water, breathing, and footsteps. Speak only the four assigned lines, in conversational Vietnamese with a consistent northern accent and accurate lip synchronization. Give each character a distinct voice and retain it in later scenes. Only the assigned speaker mouths the words. No overlapping speech, added dialogue, subtitles, narration, music, extra people, costume changes, sudden exposure shifts, dissolves, frozen ending, or fade-out.","image":"/api/files/prj_06d6f1c9496a/asset_a89400cc3de4-image.png.png","images":