Create an exactly 15-second LIVE-ACTION cinematic continuation set after the riverside episode, landscape 16:9. Begin directly in Thắng and Linh’s shared home at a later time. Do not show or repeat the riverside scene. All characters are adults. Use each fully dressed reference for both facial identity and complete wardrobe in its assigned location. Preserve faces, hairstyles, skin tones, physiques, body proportions, clothes, and accessories. Thắng and Linh remain the same recognizable people across time jumps. Environment references control architecture, furniture placement, and lighting. Clothing changes occur only across cuts. Never display reference-sheet panels, swatches, or studio backgrounds. 0.00–4.50s — LIVING TOGETHER: Open in [@Image 1] with an eye-level medium three-quarter shot, natural 40–50mm perspective. Linh wears her referenced home outfit and stirs food in a pan with a wooden spoon. Thắng, wearing his referenced home outfit, approaches from behind and gently wraps his arms around her waist over her clothing. His hands make visible contact with slight fabric compression. Linh pauses stirring, turns her head toward him with a small affectionate smile, and says in Vietnamese: “Để em nấu đã!” Keep both faces readable and their bodies clear of the hot pan. She retains control of the spoon. Thắng relaxes his hold slightly while remaining close. Use a subtle sideways dolly, warm practical illumination, soft neutral fill, and a little steam rising naturally from the food. Preserve coherent counter and utensil positions. 4.50–9.00s — THE BEDROOM: Cut to [@Image 2] at night. Both wear their assigned opaque, securely belted robes. They stand directly at the FOOT of the bed, mattress extending behind them toward the headboard. Match the distant frontal reference: camera several metres before the foot edge, centered on the bed’s long axis, chest height, level horizon, natural 35mm perspective. Frame full bodies, grounded feet, mattress edge, and headboard. Hold one continuous wide shot. A SINGLE translucent red voile sheet hangs immediately before the lens, covering the view with softly defocused weave and a transparent crimson tint. Keep the people readable through it. The fabric stays near the camera and does not surround the bed or form a canopy. Underlying room lighting is subdued warm practical illumination with faint cool window fill. Thắng rests his hands at Linh’s waist; she places hers on his shoulders. They exchange a quiet affectionate look. Linh gently pushes his shoulders; he willingly shifts backward, bends his knees, and sits on the mattress foot edge. He lightly holds her hand without pulling. Linh voluntarily steps closer and sits beside him, gently presses his shoulder again, and both recline backward side by side. Keep the movement continuous and physically grounded. Robes remain closed. No laughter, comic gestures, or dialogue. Show natural mattress compression, local bedding wrinkles, and delayed settling of hair and fabric. Cut immediately as their backs reach the mattress, before further intimacy. 9.00–12.50s — YEARS LATER: Cut to [@Image 3]. Thắng matches [@Image 4] and settles into the head chair, echoing the preceding downward movement. Preserve his exact identity. Use a medium shot slightly below seated eye level, natural 50mm perspective. Maintain the referenced table, windows, furniture, and daylight direction. The secretary matches [@Image 5]. She places a contract folder within reach and says clearly: “Thưa Tổng giám đốc, hợp đồng đây ạ.” Keep her mouth visible while speaking. Her fingers release the folder only after table contact. Thắng opens it to a prepared signature page and briefly reviews it. Keep their interaction professional. 12.50–15.00s — THE SIGNATURE: Cut close to his hand completing a short signature while his other hand stabilizes the paper. Match folder orientation and lighting. Shift focus toward his face as he looks up and says: “Được, bắt đầu thôi.” Keep his mouth sharp during speech. End with a restrained camera ease backward and the meeting continuing naturally. VIETNAMESE SPEECH: Generate native Vietnamese voices directly. Linh has a warm adult female voice, Thắng a calm adult male voice, and the secretary a distinct professional female voice. Use clear, consistent Vietnamese pronunciation, correct tones, complete words, and conversational pacing. Speak exactly the three assigned lines. Synchronize lips and jaw; only the assigned speaker mouths each line. No overlapping speech or invented words. REALISM: Real actors photographed in physical locations. Fine skin pores, slight uneven coloration, natural facial asymmetry, realistic eyes, individual hair strands, and visible fabric weave. Preserve referenced body proportions. Cotton, robes, suit fabric, wood, ceramic, metal, glass, and paper have distinct textures and restrained reflections. Folds follow gravity and contact. Ground bodies, hands, shoes, furniture, and objects with contact shadows. Keep light directions and exposure stable within each location. Natural facial shadows, controlled depth of field, stable architecture, and subtle motion blur. No beauty filters, waxy skin, plastic rendering, game shading, glowing outlines, or excessive bloom. AUDIO: Kitchen sizzling and utensils; bedroom fabric and soft mattress contact; office chair movement, paper, and pen sounds. No laughter or vocalizations in the bedroom. Restrained instrumental music may bridge the time cuts beneath dialogue. No narration, subtitles, titles, watermarks, duplicate people, intersecting bodies, floating props, wardrobe morphing, black frames, frozen ending, or fade-out.","image":"/api/files/prj_06d6f1c9496a/asset_0d9863db-0cf-frame-last.jpg","images":["/api/files/prj_06d6f1c9496a/asset_0d9863db-0cf-frame-last.jpg","/api/files/prj_06d6f1c9496a/asset_07e6b21a09de-image.png.png","/api/files/prj_06d6f1c9496a/asset_fb167ab1e30c-image.png.png","/api/files/prj_06d6f1c9496a/asset_991d5e2f354a-image.png.png","/